ready identified to the contract for sale repudiates or is otherwise in breach before risk of their loss has passed to him, the seller may to the extent of any deficiency in his effective insurance coverage treat the risk of loss as resting on the buyer for a commercially reasonable time. Definitional Cross References: “Buyer”. Section 2–103. “Conform”. Section 2–106. “Contract for sale”. Section 2–106. § 2–510ARTICLE 2. SALES"